# {Project} — Strategic Design Brief

## Interview

Questions asked ONE at a time. The agent operates as a Principal Design Director.

1. **Strategic Problem & User Need** — "What user frustration or market opportunity drives this design? Who is the primary target persona, their context of use, and emotional drivers?"
2. **Brand Identity & Aesthetic Direction** — "What brand guidelines, personality attributes (e.g., 'trustworthy & calm' vs. 'energetic & playful'), and visual design principles govern this project?"
3. **Accessibility & Regulatory Constraints** — "What accessibility standards are mandated (WCAG 2.1 AA or AAA)? What viewport targets (Mobile-first, Responsive Desktop) and platform limitations exist?"
4. **Measurable Usability Metrics** — "What quantifiable UX metrics define success (e.g., System Usability Scale >80, Task Completion Rate >95%, Time-on-Task <45s)?"

